    {"n":5,"name":"Confounds handled","score":1,"reason":"The sampling of the failures is flagged. The pass rule is not clear. The page reports 77.8% (70 of 90), a trial count. Method says every repeat of a case must pass and that intervals are over cases. A reader cannot tell which unit the pass rate uses."},
    {"n":6,"name":"Actionable next steps","score":2,"reason":"Both steps name a declaration or an inspection and say what each would settle. They could also name the trial-level failure breakdown."},
