    {"claim":"report","severity":"must_fix","finding":"The headline says 'the misses come from the urgent check'. The page's own figures do not support that. Urgent 83.3% and label 90% against 20 failures imply about 5 label-only failures and about 4 failures with both misses. Restate the headline: urgent misses are the larger share, but label misses are also a real cause. Give the counts from the measures, not from the six kept cards.","continues":"new"},
    {"claim":"c2","severity":"must_fix","finding":"c2 says 'mostly urgent-score misses, on both lookalike and plain cases' and rests it on 6 of 20 kept cards. Either show the full failure split with a computed breakdown, or soften the claim to say what the sample shows. Also clarify the T61 card. 'Label matched; Urgent score' is read as a label miss, but it may name the matched measure.","continues":"new"},
    {"claim":"report","severity":"should_fix","finding":"The pass-rate unit is unclear. The page prints 70 of 90 trials. Method says the pass rule needs every repeat of a case to pass, and that intervals are over cases. State whether 77.8% is per trial or per case, and make it match the interval.","continues":"new"},
    {"claim":"c1","severity":"should_fix","finding":"The same measure appears under two names: 'Accuracy' and 'Label matched', both 90%. 'pass rate' also appears in both lowercase and capitalised forms. Use one name for each measure.","continues":"new"},
